# 2. PROJECT OVERVIEW

## Project name
FixFlow

## Tagline
"Find Trusted Professionals. Book Services. Get Things Done."

## Problem statement

People often struggle to find reliable service providers in their local area. They may have difficulty comparing service prices, checking provider availability, scheduling appointments, tracking bookings and knowing whether a service provider is trustworthy.

Service providers also face difficulties managing customer requests, appointments, availability, payments and reviews.

FixFlow solves these problems through a centralized service booking platform.

Customers can search for services, compare providers, book appointments, make demo payments and track their service requests.

Service providers can manage their profiles, services, schedules, booking requests and earnings.

Administrators can manage users, approve providers, monitor bookings, manage categories and analyze platform activity.

## Project objectives

- Create a real-world service marketplace.
- Implement three different user roles.
- Develop secure registration and authentication.
- Build REST APIs.
- Implement relational database management.
- Create a booking and appointment system.
- Prevent duplicate appointment bookings.
- Implement payment simulation with transaction records.
- Create customer, provider and administrator dashboards.
- Build a responsive user interface.
- Demonstrate complete end-to-end workflows.

## Important business rule

A customer must not be able to access provider or administrator functionality without the appropriate permissions.

A provider must not be able to approve their own account.

An administrator must be able to approve or reject provider applications.

All important actions must be validated on the backend when the Django API is connected.

